THE [Company Name] TOP-HAT PENSION PLAN AGREEMENT

1. Establishment and Purpose

This Top-Hat Pension Plan Agreement (the "Agreement") establishes the [Company Name] Top-Hat Pension Plan (the "Plan"), a tax-qualified pension plan designed exclusively for a select group of management or highly compensated employees of [Company Name] and its affiliated companies (the "Company"). The purpose of the Plan is to provide certain eligible employees with additional retirement benefits.

2. Eligibility

To be eligible for participation in the Plan, an employee must meet the following criteria:

a. Be a customarily employed officer or employee of the Company;
b. Be among the top 35% of employees when ranked by compensation;
c. Be designated by the Company's Board of Directors or its Committee as eligible to participate in the Plan; and
d. Satisfy any additional requirements established by the Company.

3. Contributions

The Company shall make contributions to the Plan on behalf of eligible employees. The contribution amount for each employee shall be determined by the Company in its sole discretion, subject to the following limitations:

a. Contributions shall not exceed 25% of the employee's compensation;
b. Total contributions for all employees under the Plan shall not exceed the maximum amount allowed by applicable law; and
c. Contributions shall be made in accordance with the Company's nondiscrimination testing requirements.

4. Investment Options

The Plan shall offer a variety of investment options, including but not limited to:

a. Stocks, bonds, and other equity securities;
b. Mutual funds;
c. Exchange-traded funds (ETFs);
d. Real estate investment trusts (REITs);
e. Company stock; and
f. Other investment vehicles as permitted by law.

5. Distribution Rules

Distributions from the Plan shall be made in accordance with the following rules:

a. Distributions shall begin no earlier than age 55 and no later than April 1 of the calendar year following the calendar year in which the employee attains age 72;
b. Distributions shall be made in the form of a lump sum or periodic payments, as elected by the participant;
